{"record": "apparatus", "feature": "0037", "machine": "m2max-32gb", "harness": "claude-code 2.1.233", "endpoint": "config/agent.env at 49152, one server for every probe", "question": "the largest prompt Claude Code will send against a declared context, and whether declaring the whole served context is safe", "instrument": "scripts/promptwall.sh \u2014 padding of an exact served-token count, then one `claude -p` per size against a fresh CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR", "refusal": "`Prompt is too long`, exit 1, and nothing reaches the server: the check is the harness's own and costs no ingest", "counted_tokens": "padding_tokens plus 3,508, the preamble and instruction the same tool set spends \u2014 measured by a probe of one padding token, which the server counted at 3,509", "processed_tokens": "the server's llamacpp:prompt_tokens_total delta, which counts what it had to process and not what it was sent: a probe that reuses a cached prefix processes far less than it counted", "padding": "one word stream, so every size is a prefix of every larger one and the server's cache carries across probes. Its density is 4.1 characters a token and no other density was tried, so a harness counting characters rather than tokens would not be distinguished here.", "brackets": "each wall is bracketed between the largest padding sent and the smallest refused; the step is 250 tokens at three of the four and 500 at 32,768"}
